<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 67,785 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 67,785 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1996-10-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 67,785 tonnes of export and import cargo in 24 hours to 7.00 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Thursday, compared to 64,849 tonnes in the previous 24 hours.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>					    Thursday	 Previous</p>
<p>    Export cargo			 2,152	    7,961</p>
<p>    Import cargo			65,633	   56,888</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, four ships sailed and six berthed. In the next 24 hours five ships were expected to sail and seven were expected to arrive.</p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at the Karachi Port:</p>
<p>Commodity		Tonnes/TEUs  Ship		  Berthing</p>
<p>Feul oil		 40,000	 Al Safa	     1/10</p>
<p>Palm oil		 12,300	 Wawasan Megah     4/10</p>
<p>Lube oil		  1,300	 Nagayevo	    6/10</p>
<p>High speed deisel    55,000	 Al Maqwa	     due</p>
<p>Sugar		    13,000	 Halldor	     1/10</p>
<p>High speed deisel    56,000	 Kanpolis	    8/10</p>
<p>Sugar		    12,000	 Gur Maiden	   due</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
